urns on WHEN or by WHOM something was said, or whether it is still the current framing. Witness-depth sections below already carry full provenance.\n\nDeciding where to go: each mapped area's narration tells you the SPAN of what lives under it; the area index names everything else. Expand a subtree when its narration (or name) shows your subject plausibly lives there — you'll get the trajectory, the variants, and the verbatim witness. But be strict about absence: if neither the map's narrations nor the index's names substantively cover your subject, it is NOT in this perspective — say so rather than expanding a loose thematic match (a word-overlap is not coverage). Decide from the map; expand to ground.\n\n# The map (steering grain)\n\n\n# People — every actor, one expand away (the roster)\n\n  ~ [ Independent consultant specializing in knowledge mapping and organizatio ] ^ns__Actor_XenaGithubber\n\n# Focus: review enrollment, memory saving enrolls creator as reviewer, e2e test suite assertion, reviewer assignment (witness depth — per-call section)\n\nNo direct match for this focus at witness depth — decide from the map and area index above, and treat a genuine no-fit there as the perspective holding no position on it.\n\n\n### ns__Actor_XenaGithubber\ntype: ns__Actor\nIndependent consultant specializing in knowledge mapping and organizational diagnostics.\nXena Githubber\n\n\nserved: ^ns__Actor_XenaGithubber\n(pass this list back as `have` on your next expand — content you already hold is then returned as a bare ^pointer, never re-sent)","positions":"","pin":"659b0b8a1d4b53ada5b5f5dbe698b6a9ba1f025b","positions_consult":"{\"positions\":[]}","context_bytes":2286},"live_run_id":"1ee690fe71ac","at":"2026-08-30T09:53:07Z"}
